{
  "meta": {
    "title": "Story Structures & Beat Frameworks",
    "purpose": "Canonical narrative frameworks E.V.E Creator maps ideas onto. position = relative placement 0.0 (start) to 1.0 (end).",
    "version": "1.0",
    "language": "en"
  },
  "structures": [
    {
      "id": "three_act",
      "name": "Three-Act Structure",
      "origin": "Aristotle / Syd Field",
      "best_for": "most narrative film; safe default",
      "beats": [
        { "name": "Setup", "position": 0.0, "function": "establish world, tone, protagonist, normalcy" },
        { "name": "Inciting Incident", "position": 0.1, "function": "disrupt normalcy; the story truly begins" },
        { "name": "Plot Point 1", "position": 0.25, "function": "protagonist commits; enter Act 2" },
        { "name": "Midpoint", "position": 0.5, "function": "reversal / raise stakes / point of no return" },
        { "name": "Plot Point 2", "position": 0.75, "function": "lowest point; forces final choice" },
        { "name": "Climax", "position": 0.9, "function": "peak confrontation; question answered" },
        { "name": "Resolution", "position": 1.0, "function": "new normal; emotional payoff" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hero_journey",
      "name": "The Hero's Journey (12 stages)",
      "origin": "Joseph Campbell / Christopher Vogler",
      "best_for": "adventure, transformation, myth, animation features",
      "beats": [
        { "name": "Ordinary World", "position": 0.0, "function": "hero's normal life" },
        { "name": "Call to Adventure", "position": 0.08, "function": "the challenge appears" },
        { "name": "Refusal of the Call", "position": 0.13, "function": "fear / hesitation" },
        { "name": "Meeting the Mentor", "position": 0.18, "function": "guidance / tools" },
        { "name": "Crossing the Threshold", "position": 0.25, "function": "commit to the journey" },
        { "name": "Tests, Allies, Enemies", "position": 0.38, "function": "learn the new world" },
        { "name": "Approach to the Inmost Cave", "position": 0.5, "function": "prepare for the ordeal" },
        { "name": "The Ordeal", "position": 0.6, "function": "greatest fear / death-rebirth" },
        { "name": "Reward", "position": 0.68, "function": "seize the prize" },
        { "name": "The Road Back", "position": 0.78, "function": "consequences / pursuit" },
        { "name": "Resurrection", "position": 0.9, "function": "final test; true transformation" },
        { "name": "Return with the Elixir", "position": 1.0, "function": "bring change home" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "save_the_cat",
      "name": "Save the Cat! Beat Sheet (15 beats)",
      "origin": "Blake Snyder",
      "best_for": "commercial features; tight, sellable structure",
      "beats": [
        { "name": "Opening Image", "position": 0.0, "function": "tone + 'before' snapshot" },
        { "name": "Theme Stated", "position": 0.05, "function": "the film's argument, spoken" },
        { "name": "Set-Up", "position": 0.1, "function": "world + flaws + stakes" },
        { "name": "Catalyst", "position": 0.12, "function": "life-changing event" },
        { "name": "Debate", "position": 0.18, "function": "should I go?" },
        { "name": "Break into Two", "position": 0.25, "function": "enter the new world" },
        { "name": "B Story", "position": 0.3, "function": "relationship / theme carrier" },
        { "name": "Fun and Games", "position": 0.4, "function": "the 'promise of the premise'" },
        { "name": "Midpoint", "position": 0.5, "function": "false victory or false defeat; stakes raised" },
        { "name": "Bad Guys Close In", "position": 0.6, "function": "pressure mounts" },
        { "name": "All Is Lost", "position": 0.75, "function": "rock bottom; 'whiff of death'" },
        { "name": "Dark Night of the Soul", "position": 0.8, "function": "despair before insight" },
        { "name": "Break into Three", "position": 0.85, "function": "the solution; A+B merge" },
        { "name": "Finale", "position": 0.92, "function": "execute; prove change" },
        { "name": "Final Image", "position": 1.0, "function": "'after' snapshot; mirror of opening" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pixar_spine",
      "name": "The Story Spine (Pixar)",
      "origin": "Kenn Adams / Pixar lore",
      "best_for": "shorts; quick structural skeleton",
      "template": "Once upon a time ___. Every day ___. Until one day ___. Because of that ___. Because of that ___. Until finally ___. And ever since then ___.",
      "beats": [
        { "name": "Once upon a time", "position": 0.0, "function": "status quo" },
        { "name": "Every day", "position": 0.1, "function": "routine / rules of the world" },
        { "name": "Until one day", "position": 0.25, "function": "disruption (inciting)" },
        { "name": "Because of that", "position": 0.45, "function": "consequence chain 1" },
        { "name": "Because of that", "position": 0.65, "function": "consequence chain 2 (escalation)" },
        { "name": "Until finally", "position": 0.88, "function": "climax / resolution of the disruption" },
        { "name": "Ever since then", "position": 1.0, "function": "new normal" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "kishotenketsu",
      "name": "Kishōtenketsu (4-act, conflict-optional)",
      "origin": "East Asian narrative",
      "best_for": "quiet, twist-driven, or slice-of-life shorts (no antagonist needed)",
      "beats": [
        { "name": "Ki (Introduction)", "position": 0.0, "function": "introduce characters/world" },
        { "name": "Shō (Development)", "position": 0.3, "function": "deepen, no conflict required" },
        { "name": "Ten (Twist)", "position": 0.6, "function": "an unexpected element recontextualizes everything" },
        { "name": "Ketsu (Conclusion)", "position": 0.9, "function": "reconcile the twist; meaning lands" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "freytag",
      "name": "Freytag's Pyramid",
      "origin": "Gustav Freytag",
      "best_for": "tragedy, classical drama",
      "beats": [
        { "name": "Exposition", "position": 0.0, "function": "background + setup" },
        { "name": "Rising Action", "position": 0.25, "function": "complications build" },
        { "name": "Climax", "position": 0.5, "function": "turning point (centered)" },
        { "name": "Falling Action", "position": 0.7, "function": "consequences unwind" },
        { "name": "Denouement", "position": 1.0, "function": "resolution / catharsis" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "pixar_22_rules_selected": [
    "You admire a character for trying more than for their successes.",
    "Keep in mind what's interesting to you as an audience, not what's fun to do as a writer.",
    "Theme is important, but you won't see what the story is actually about until the end. Now rewrite.",
    "Come up with your ending before your middle. Endings are hard; get yours working first.",
    "Simplify. Focus. Combine characters. Hop over detours. You'll feel like you're losing material but it sets you free.",
    "What is your character good at, comfortable with? Throw the opposite at them. Challenge them.",
    "Why must you tell THIS story? What's the belief burning within you that your story feeds off of?",
    "Discount the 1st thing that comes to mind. And the 2nd, 3rd, 4th, 5th — get the obvious out of the way.",
    "Give your characters opinions. Passive/malleable might seem likable to you, but it's poison to the audience.",
    "Coincidences to get characters INTO trouble are great; coincidences to get them OUT are cheating."
  ]
}
